		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: force and torque calculation in Runge_kutta]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=16966#p16966"><![CDATA[
Agreed, this method is at most first order if your forces are nonzero and depend on the bodies state.<br>But think of the case, for instance, of free fall.  The only force is gravity, which is constant anyway.  So the method would still be 4th order.<br>The extra stability comes from integrating the gyroscopic nonlinearity at higher order (Euler blows up if the object is spinning).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5718">dneckels</a> — Wed Jan 13, 2010 3:59 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
